================================================================================
6. HEALTH DATA AND BIOMETRIC INFORMATION
================================================================================

Digital Saver records health-related measurements, which may include heart rate,
heart-rate variability, blood oxygen saturation, activity, motion, and sleep
timing. Such measurements are sensitive personal information. Because that is
what they are, the following applies in addition to the restrictions above:

  (a) Health data belongs to the person it describes. Cambric claims no
      ownership of any measurement recorded by, or on behalf of, a user.

  (b) Local by default. The Software stores readings on the user's own device.
      Running the core application requires no account and transmits no reading
      to Cambric.

  (c) The optional assistant. If a user chooses to use the built-in assistant,
      the content of the questions they ask, together with the health context
      they attach to them, is sent to a third-party language model provider for
      processing. This is off unless the user uses the feature, and it is
      disclosed in the Software and its documentation. Deployments must not
      enable or encourage it without saying so plainly.

  (d) No secondary use. Cambric does not sell health data, and does not use it
      for advertising, insurance, employment, credit, or any other purpose
      beyond returning it to the person it came from.

  (e) Your obligations. If you deploy the Software, you are the controller of
      any health data it collects for the purposes of applicable data-protection
      law. You must obtain informed consent where required, keep the data
      secure, provide access and deletion on request, and retain it no longer
      than necessary.

  (f) Deletion. Uninstalling the Software removes its stored readings. Where a
      deployment holds data elsewhere, deletion must be honoured there too.

================================================================================
7. MEDICAL & SAFETY DISCLAIMER (CRITICAL)
================================================================================

THE SOFTWARE IS AN EXPERIMENTAL CONSUMER WELLNESS AND PROTOTYPING PLATFORM.
IT IS NOT A CERTIFIED MEDICAL DEVICE AND HAS NOT BEEN EVALUATED BY THE EGYPTIAN
DRUG AUTHORITY (EDA), THE FDA, THE CE MARKING SYSTEM, OR ANY OTHER RECOGNISED
MEDICAL REGULATORY BODY.

MEASUREMENTS PRODUCED BY THE SOFTWARE ARE ESTIMATES FROM A WRIST-WORN SENSOR.
THEY ARE AFFECTED BY MOTION, SKIN CONTACT, LIGHT, TEMPERATURE, AND SENSOR
PLACEMENT. THEY HAVE NOT BEEN VALIDATED AGAINST CLINICAL REFERENCE EQUIPMENT.

THE SOFTWARE MUST NOT BE USED FOR:

  - Clinical diagnostic purposes, medical treatment, or triage decisions
  - Sole-means emergency alert or life-critical monitoring
  - Substitution for licensed professional medical consultation
  - Any decision that could result in injury if a reading were wrong

The emergency and fall-detection features, where present, are conveniences that
depend on a functioning device, a charged battery, a working radio link, and
correct configuration by the user. They can fail, and must never be relied on as
the only way help would be called.

If you are unwell, or a reading concerns you, seek qualified medical advice.
Do not delay it because of anything the Software showed you.

